# Project governance

The source of truth for task state is `.cursor/management/tasks.json`. Conversation progress is not completion.

- The CTO agent is the only role that assigns or reassigns tasks in the registry.
- Specialists may recommend changes. They must not edit `tasks.json` or `team.json`.
- A task is completed only after the verification commands have been run and the result is recorded.
- Do not mark work complete from an agent's summary alone.
- Do not start a task whose dependencies are not `completed`.
- Do not give two active tasks the same write path. Active statuses are `assigned` and `in_progress`.

Protected without explicit user approval:

- `.env` and any secret value
- `ros_server.db` and other live database files
- rewriting an already applied migration revision
- deleting `legacy_players` or player-owned rows

```text
Bad:  set RO-009 status to completed because the schema "looks safe"
Good: leave RO-009 ready until a review report cites the files that were read
```
